  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Total federal contract obligations to West Virginia are $1.1B in FY2026 to date. Award count stands at 3,473 and average award size is $312K. Obligations fell 42.3% year over year. Annual obligations peaked at $2B in FY24 and then declined to $1.9B in FY25 and $1.1B in FY26. The Department of Energy is the largest buyer with $224M, followed by the Department of Veterans Affairs with $208M and the Department of Justice with $196M. LEIDOS, INC. is the top vendor at $103M, followed by SAWTOOTH CONSTRUCTION JV II LLC at $60.7M and IMPRES TECHNOLOGY SOLUTIONS, INC at $50.5M. Major industry categories include Other Computer Related Services at $155M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) at $135M, with Commercial and Institutional Building Construction at $117M. These figures are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial for the fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What drove the year-over-year decline in obligations?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 42.3% year over year. Annual totals show a peak of $2B in FY24, then $1.9B in FY25 and $1.1B in FY26, indicating a sharp reduction in obligation volume this fiscal year. The drop is reflected across top buyers and industries, with major agencies like the Department of Energy at $224M and the Department of Veterans Affairs at $208M still accounting for large shares of the reduced total."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where is federal spending concentrated in West Virginia?",
        "body": "Spending is concentrated in a few agencies and industries. The top three buying agencies are the Department of Energy at $224M, the Department of Veterans Affairs at $208M, and the Department of Justice at $196M. Key industry buckets are Other Computer Related Services at $155M, R&D in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $135M, and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction at $117M."
      }
    ]
  },
